<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9094" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">col-lŏcŭplēto</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conl-</span></b> ),
			āvi, 1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make very rich</i>,
				<i>to enrich</i> (prob. only in the foll. exs.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">se,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Heaut. 2, 3, 17</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to embellish</i>,
				<i>enrich</i>, <i>adorn</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rei honestandae et collocupletandae
					causā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 2, 18, 28</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
